--- body ---
## Context

Second tranche (tracker 0550): the conductor exists and runs only the
tick. N × P0 elect exactly one conductor through the lease row; the
pipeline does not multiply with N.

## Relevant files

- SPEC.md §5.2.5: lease UPDATE idiom, UUID holder, TTL 20 s = 2 ×
  heartbeat, election check 10 s, migration gate < 30 s; the CAS
  commit-guard idiom; orphan rules (stdin EOF, holder re-check between
  micro-batches).

## Actions

1. Lease acquisition/renewal on the injected clock; renewal decoupled
   from stage progress.
2. Election check in every P0; the winner runs the tick from tranche 1.
3. Orphan repairs: exit on stdin EOF; holder re-verification hook (used
   from tranche 3 on).

## Test

- Red first: two P0 processes on one data directory — exactly one
  conductor; kill -9 it twice, another takes over within TTL + cadence
  (virtual time), per the SPEC soak clause.

## Verification

- [x] Deposed-but-running conductor's conditional UPDATE writes nothing
      — the race is constructed, not asserted: A holds, virtual time passes
      the TTL, B's UPDATE succeeds and B becomes holder, then A — which does
      not know yet — runs its own conditional UPDATE. Zero rows changed, and
      the write body never executes, which is stronger than a rollback: a
      guard that ran the body and undid it would still have sent whatever
      the body sent. Positive control beside it — the same statement with
      `holder = :uuid` removed changes 1 row.
- [ ] Failover duplicate work bounded per SPEC's honest R13 restatement
      — HELD SHORT DELIBERATELY. R13's restatement has two halves. "Never
      committed twice" is demonstrated, by the CAS guard above. "Duplicate
      compute bounded by one embed batch plus one in-flight document's
      re-fetch and re-segmentation per failover" cannot be: there is no
      embed batch and no document fetch or segmentation in the fork yet —
      tranches 3 and 4 — so there is nothing whose duplication could be
      counted. The mechanism the bound rests on is built and tested; the
      bound itself is not measurable until its subject exists, and the box
      stays unticked rather than being read down to the half that was.

## Invariants

- Query path stays write-free; upstream tests green.
- [x] Verified: 7 new files, 1 834 insertions, 0 deletions — no existing
      file touched, so the query path is unchanged structurally rather than
      by inspection. A follower's `poll()` reaches no ledger statement at
      all, tested. Suite 979 → 1 020 passing, 7 skipped throughout.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Election + lease merged on a fork branch, soak test green
      — `MinhHaDuong/zoteus` branch `tranche-2-conductor-election`, tip
      a00091b, branched from tranche 1's e563570. Read as "landed on a fork
      branch", per 0551's precedent: no PR against the fork's `main` or
      `base-v1.12.0`, deliberately — the branch accumulates and tranche 3
      branches from this tip. Soak green: three P0s on one data directory,
      each its own connection, `kill -9` twice, a different survivor each
      time, handover within TTL + cadence in virtual time.
